+MCS-51 XDATA ownership metadata
+=============================
+
+--xdata-ownership writes <output-basename>.xdata.json when the MCS-51
+compiler emits assembly. The option is disabled by default and does not
+require --debug. For example:
+
+  sdcc -mmcs51 --model-large --debug --xdata-ownership -c input.c
+
+This is representation only, not an overlay allocator. All existing area
+directives, allocation order, assembler/debug symbols, instructions,
+calling conventions and startup routines are unchanged. Nothing is added
+to the assembler object or the linker command. Without the option no
+sidecar is written; an old sidecar is not removed. Build systems must keep
+metadata and its corresponding compilation artifacts together, reject
+stale inputs and archive metadata separately if needed.
+
+Version 1 schema
+----------------
+
+The top-level JSON object contains version (integer 1), module (compiler
+module name), and objects (an array in declaration emission order).
+Each entry describes an actually emitted XDATA declaration or absolute
+equate, after unused and external-only declarations have been filtered:
+
+  symbol             assembler spelling
+  name               compiler spelling
+  owner              lexical/allocated function name, or null
+  owner_symbol       function entry symbol, or null
+  class              one of the storage classes below
+  area               assembler area identifier, without attributes
+  cdb_key            corresponding debug key, even without --debug
+  size               object size including any flexible array extension
+  absolute           true for explicitly addressed objects
+  address            absolute address, or zero for relocatable objects
+  owner_reentrant    function is reentrant or --stack-auto is in effect
+  owner_isr          function is an interrupt handler
+  address_taken      compiler IR address-taken fact, NOT an escape proof
+
+The maps described are XSEG, XISEG and XABS. An absolute equate describes
+an object's width, not a new reservation of that many bytes. XINIT bytes
+are initializer CODE, not an additional XDATA object. Final relocatable
+addresses remain a linker fact. Consumers must correlate the symbol,
+area, size and debug key with the actual linked artifacts.
+
+Storage classes
+---------------
+
+GLOBAL                  ordinary object without a function owner
+FILE_STATIC             translation-unit static object
+STATIC_LOCAL            retained object with a lexical function owner
+LOCAL                   automatic function-owned home
+PARAM_CALLER_WRITTEN     non-register parameter allocated for the callee
+FIRST_ARGUMENT_HOME     home for the normal first register argument
+REGISTER_ARGUMENT_HOME  home for an additional register argument
+COMPILER_TEMP           IR/AST/compiler-generated temporary
+INLINE_RETURN_HOME      AST home joining returns of an inlined function
+UNKNOWN                 ownership/class cannot be established
+
+The AST provenance bits only annotate new temporaries and inlined return
+homes. They are never inputs to allocation or code generation; reusing
+the pre-existing cdef flag would not guarantee this property. Copies of
+symbols retain their provenance, while localof describes the containing
+function after inlining. Inlined formal locals belong to that containing
+function, not to a separately activated callee.
+
+A register argument need not have a physical home. Reentrant and
+--stack-auto stack objects are not invented as static XDATA reservations.
+Any retained XDATA objects associated with such functions carry the flags
+above. Existing register spills in DATA and normal register return values
+are likewise outside this manifest. Runtime source compiled with this
+option follows the same rules; prebuilt or assembly-only runtime objects
+have no implied ownership metadata. Missing metadata must remain unknown.
+
+Ownership is not lifetime
+-------------------------
+
+No class grants overlay permission. In particular, a caller may write a
+PARAM_CALLER_WRITTEN home before callee activation. STATIC_LOCAL persists
+between calls. ISR and reentrant storage requires independent concurrency
+reasoning. address_taken=false proves neither initialization nor nonescape.
+Indirect calls, recursion, nesting, relocation references, startup ranges,
+region fences and private pointer contracts require downstream proofs.
+
+Consumers must fail closed on unrecognized schema/classes, missing owners,
+unbound objects, stale sidecars or unsupported storage. This format contains
+no call graph, call-site frame use, physical placement or eligibility bit.
+
+Regression
+----------
+
+Build a stock control and patched compiler with the same configuration,
+retaining the executable name sdcc so sibling tool lookup is unchanged:
+
+  python3 support/regression/test-xdata-ownership.py \
+    --sdcc /path/to/patched/bin/sdcc --control /path/to/control/bin/sdcc
+
+The test checks disabled/enabled assembly, object, debug and linked-image
+identity; first/caller/register-bank parameters; automatic, static, global,
+address-taken, pointer, aggregate, array and inline-return storage;
+reentrant/stack-auto/ISR cases; external symbols; debug-off output;
+initialized and absolute XDATA; and an unwritable metadata destination.
+It does not run a target, allocate overlays or claim whole-program safety.
